    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's past references in the public sector, such as the digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia, our company's can draw on these experiences to tailor a solution that meets the City of Belval's objectives. our company's consortium partners, including EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., can provide specialized expertise in areas like sovereign cloud hosting, legal AI, and green IT, which align with the City of Belval's goals of reducing environmental footprint and improving service quality. As of 2024, our company's available project management capacity is 60%, allowing our company's to allocate sufficient resources to this project. our company's governance practices, including the use of RAID logs, decision logs, change request processes, and steering committees, will ensure transparent and structured communication with the City of Belval's throughout the project lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the City of Belval's objectives specifically, our company's can propose a phased approach, starting with an inception and design phase to understand current administrative services and identify areas for improvement. an inception and design phase to understand current administrative services and identify areas for improvement would be followed by a pilot or MVP phase to test solutions, and then a full rollout phase to implement the new services. our company's change management capabilities, including dedicated change managers, training delivery, and user adoption tracking, will support the City of Belval's agents in adapting to the new services. By combining our company's public sector experience, project management methodologies, consortium partners' expertise, and governance practices, our company's can submit a comprehensive tender response that addresses the City of Belval's objectives and requirements, while also ensuring a low-to-medium risk appetite and adherence to regulatory requirements like GDPR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a response time < 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, API integration with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories. Hosting must be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, with no dependency on non-European suppliers. Can our current technology stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do our propose? Based on our context, our can meet some of the client's requirements. our technical expertise includes API integration, which can be used to integrate with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories using standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP. our have experience with identity providers like Active Directory/LDAP and Keycloak, which can be used for user directory integration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For hosting, our have experience with cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud. our can deploy our solution on cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud to meet the sovereignty constraint. Regarding performance, our typical benchmarks include a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is below the required 2 seconds. However, our need to ensure that our solution can scale to meet the required availability of 99.9%. our experience with containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s), as well as monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana, can help our achieve scale. To propose an architecture, I would suggest a cloud-native approach using containers and orchestration with Kubernetes (K8s). our can design a microservices-based architecture that integrates with the required systems via APIs and ensures high availability and scalability. our experience with Terraform and Ansible as IaC tools can help our automate the deployment and management of the infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I must note that our context does not explicitly mention civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, or specific user directories. Therefore, our would need to assess the specific integration requirements and ensure that our API integration capabilities can meet the specific integration requirements. Additionally, while our have experience with SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, our need to verify that our current technology stack does not depend on non-European suppliers, which could be a constraint. our context mentions HashiCorp Vault as a secrets management tool, which is a US-based company, but our also mention CyberArk Conjur as an alternative, which might be more suitable given the sovereignty constraint. In summary, while our current technology stack can meet some of the client's requirements, our need to conduct a thorough assessment of the specific integration needs and ensure that our solution does not depend on non-European suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "With careful planning and design, our can propose an architecture that meets the required performance, availability, and sovereignty constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender demands strict GDPR compliance (EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside EU, encryption of sensitive data) and explicability of AI recommendations. All decisions must be validated by an agent, with no automation without explicit validation. What security controls and regulatory compliance measures do we need to implement, considering we current certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with EU regulatory frameworks? To address The tender demands for strict GDPR compliance and explicability of AI recommendations, we can leverage we existing certifications and capabilities. we ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, demonstrates we commitment to security and data protection. Additionally, having a GDPR Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and reachable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it ensures we have the necessary expertise in-house to navigate GDPR requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For EU-only hosting and no data transfer outside EU, we standard data residency policy already specifies that data should reside within EU, aligning with specifies. To further reinforce specifies, we can utilize we experience with SecNumCloud projects, ensuring that any infrastructure used for hosting meets the high security standards expected. Encryption of sensitive data is a critical component of GDPR compliance. While we context does not explicitly mention encryption methods, we ISO 27001 certification and experience with risk management (ISO 27005) imply that we have the capability to implement appropriate encryption measures to protect sensitive data. Regarding explicability of AI recommendations and ensuring all decisions are validated by an agent without automation, we AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. our AI security controls can help ensure that AI-driven recommendations are transparent and reliable." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, we model isolation approach, where end-users do not have direct access to models but interact through an inference API, can facilitate the validation process by agents. we audit capabilities, including all queries being logged with immutability ensured through append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining, and real-time SIEM integration, will help in maintaining a compliant and secure environment. This is crucial for monitoring and demonstrating GDPR compliance, especially considering we ability to conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) with an average duration of 3 weeks. Given we experience with EU regulatory frameworks such as the GDPR, NIS2 Directive, and eIDAS, we are well-positioned to ensure that all regulatory requirements are met. we capability to provide anonymization tools, such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, can further support GDPR compliance by ensuring that personal data is appropriately protected. In summary, by leveraging we current certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with EU regulatory frameworks, we can implement the necessary security controls and regulatory compliance measures to meet The tender demands for strict GDPR compliance and explicability of AI recommendations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires a solution that respects the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), does not automate decisions without explicit agent validation, and provides explainable recommendations. Considering our company's legal standing, procurement experience across EU jurisdictions, IP model, insurance, standard contractual clauses, and AI regulatory posture, what are the key legal risks our company's should flag, and are our company's compliant with the key legal risks we should flag? Based on the provided context, our company's has experience with public procurement in various EU jurisdictions, including Italy, France, Germany, Belgium, and EU institutions. our company's legal standing is that of a Società a responsabilità limitata (S.r.l.), with no exclusion grounds applicable." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) compliance, our company's company context indicates that our company's have a standard legal basis for data processing under Article 6(1)(e) of the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), which pertains to the performance of tasks in the public interest. our company's also have a Data Protection Agreement (DPA) template version 3.2 and offer support for Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs). The requirement for not automating decisions without explicit agent validation aligns with our company's AI regulatory knowledge, which includes awareness of prohibited AI practices and the importance of human oversight. Specifically, our company's have a policy of no automated decision-making without human validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For explainable recommendations, while there is no direct mention of a policy of no automated decision-making without human validation in our company context, our company's experience with public procurement and provision of services to EU institutions suggests that our company's should be able to provide transparent and understandable solutions. Key legal risks flagged include ensuring the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) compliance, particularly in the context of cross-border data flows within EU (though our company context notes that SCCs are not applicable for intra-EU operations), and adhering to AI regulatory requirements. our company's also need to ensure that our company's subcontractors, if any, comply with these regulations. Given our company's experience, legal standing, and policies regarding the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), AI, and intellectual property, our company's appear to be compliant with The City of Belval requirements for the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) respect, non-automated decision-making, and explainable recommendations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it is essential to conduct a thorough review of the specific contract terms and ensure that all aspects of the project adhere to the City of Belval's requirements for GDPR respect, non-automated decision-making, and explainable recommendations and our company's company policies." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for this project is 3 million euros over 4 years, with annual exploitation costs that must remain within the local authority's budgetary capacities. Given our pricing model, current financial position, and cost estimation parameters as of 2024, what is our projected margin on this project, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose to meet these budgetary constraints? Based on the provided context, our target gross margin percentage is 28 percent. However, to calculate The global budget for this project our need to consider the total contract value and our estimated costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for this project is 3 million euros over 4 years, which translates to approximately 750,000 euros per year. our pricing model includes standard daily rates for various professionals, but without knowing the exact scope of work, it's challenging to estimate the total cost of this project accurately. Nevertheless, assuming our can maintain The global budget for this project, our projected revenue from this project would be 3 million euros, and our projected cost would be 2,160,000 euros (3,000,000 * (1 - 0.28)). As for cost-optimization strategies to meet the budgetary constraints, our can consider absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors if there's a 10 percent budget reduction. For more significant reductions, our might need to reduce the project scope by removing optional modules or reducing training days." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our current financial position and the debt-to-equity ratio of 0.42, our have some flexibility to manage our costs and potentially offer competitive pricing while maintaining The global budget for this project. However, without more detailed information on the project scope and requirements, it's difficult to provide a precise cost estimate and optimization strategy. our minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18 percent, which could serve as a basis for negotiations if needed, to ensure our can still deliver this project while meeting the budgetary constraints. By carefully managing our costs, renegotiating rates with subcontractors, and potentially adjusting the project scope, our can work towards achieving a mutually beneficial agreement that satisfies both The global budget for this project and the client's budgetary requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval seeks an AI solution that provides intelligent assistance to agents, facilitates access to information, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and integrates with existing systems. Considering our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, performance benchmarks, past AI use cases, and known trade-offs as of 2024, what AI components and innovation strategy can our design to meet these requirements? To address The City of Belval requirements, our AI solution will leverage the Mistral 7B Instruct model, our preferred sovereign model, due to the Mistral 7B Instruct model, our preferred sovereign model strong French-language performance, EU origin, and self-hostable nature. the Mistral 7B Instruct model, our preferred sovereign model will be fine-tuned using our established methods, such as LoRA or QLoRA, on a domain-specific corpus to improve answer quality and adapt to the administrative context. our Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities will be utilized to facilitate access to information and reduce processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By integrating RAG with our preferred vector store, Qdrant, our can efficiently retrieve relevant information from existing systems and provide accurate answers. The hybrid retrieval strategy, combining dense vector and BM25 sparse approaches, will ensure a high level of precision. To address the need for explainability and transparency, our will implement our XAI methods, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP, and LIME. our XAI methods, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP, and LIME will provide insights into the decision-making process and ensure that the solution is trustworthy and compliant with regulatory requirements. our past experience in delivering AI solutions for public administration, such as the regulatory document Q&A assistant, will serve as a foundation for this project. our will build upon our knowledge of integrating AI systems with existing practices and ensuring seamless continuity of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of innovation strategy, our will focus on progressive deployment, starting with a pilot phase and gradually generalizing the solution. progressive deployment will allow our to test and refine the system while minimizing risks and ensuring that the system meets The City of Belval specific needs. To mitigate known trade-offs, such as explicability vs. performance, our will carefully balance the level of model complexity and transparency. our average accuracy gain from fine-tuning is around 12%, which will help improve answer quality while maintaining a reasonable level of explainability. By combining our LLM expertise, RAG capabilities, and explainability tools with a progressive deployment strategy, our can design an AI solution that effectively addresses the City of Belval's requirements and provides intelligent assistance to agents while ensuring transparency, trustworthiness, and regulatory compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to limit The City of Belval environmental footprint by reducing energetic consumption and using infrastructures with low carbon impact. Given The City of Belval current EcoVadis rating, carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs as of 2024, how can The City of Belval propose a solution that contributes to these environmental goals while ensuring the quality of service expected? As the CSR & Sustainability Officer of Nexus Engineering S.r.l., the CSR & Sustainability Officer of Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose a solution that aligns with these environmental goals. Given The City of Belval current EcoVadis Silver rating and a score of 62, The City of Belval have a solid foundation for sustainability. The City of Belval carbon footprint stands at 148 Scope 1 and 2 tCO2e as of the last bilan carbone conducted in 2023, and The City of Belval aim to reach net zero by 2040." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To contribute to reducing energetic consumption, The City of Belval can leverage The City of Belval green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both based in France and utilizing 100% renewable energy. leverage aligns with the goal of using infrastructures with low carbon impact. The City of Belval digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, can help minimize energetic consumption. Moreover, The City of Belval typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which demonstrates The City of Belval capability to optimize energy use. By integrating these practices into the proposed solution for The City of Belval, we can ensure a significant reduction in energetic consumption while maintaining the quality of service expected. It's also important to address potential sustainability trade-offs, such as the balance between high availability and energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval standard resolution for the balance between high availability and energy consumption involves using low-power standby modes with less than 90 seconds wake-up time, which is compatible with SLA requirements. By proposing a solution that incorporates these sustainable practices and technologies, The City of Belval can support The City of Belval in achieving these environmental goals while ensuring the quality and reliability of the services provided. Additionally, The City of Belval commitment to social responsibilities, such as gender equality, disabled worker integration, and accessibility standards, ensures that the proposed solution for the City of Belval will be inclusive and respectful of all stakeholders. The City of Belval AI ethics principles, including human oversight, non-discriminatory outputs, transparency, and the right to contest AI-generated suggestions, further ensure that any AI-driven components of the proposed solution for the City of Belval will be aligned with ethical standards, contributing to a trustworthy and responsible service. Overall, by leveraging The City of Belval existing sustainability capabilities, green technologies, and commitment to social and ethical responsibilities, The City of Belval can propose a solution that not only meets but exceeds The City of Belval expectations for environmental stewardship and quality of service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "**Executive Summary** Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's administrative services. proposes leverages Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience in public sector projects, AI solutions, and commitment to sustainability, security, and regulatory compliance. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. aim to enhance the efficiency of administrative services, improve service quality, and reduce processing times while ensuring explicability, transparency, and human oversight. **Understanding of Requirements** the City of Belval's seeks an AI solution that assists agents in agents daily missions by facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure high availability, and comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR. Additionally, the City of Belval's emphasizes the importance of sovereignty, environmental sustainability, and social responsibility. **Proposed Solution** To address the City of Belval's objectives, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose a phased approach: 1. **Inception and Design Phase**: Utilize Nexus Engineering S.r.l. project management methodologies (PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, SAFe) to understand current administrative services and identify areas for improvement. 2. **Pilot Phase**: Deploy a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system using the Mistral 7B Instruct model, fine-tuned with LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus. a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system will be integrated with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. preferred vector store, Qdrant, to facilitate access to information. 3. **Full Rollout Phase**: Implement The solution across all administrative services, ensuring high availability (99.9%) and scalability using containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes). Nexus Engineering S.r.l. technical architecture will utilize: * API integration with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories using standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP. * SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU (e.g., Outscale, OVHcloud) for hosting. * HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur for secrets management. * Terraform and Ansible as IaC tools for deployment automation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explicability and transparency, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement XAI methods, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP, and LIME. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. AI security controls will include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution will comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR, ensuring data residency within the EU, encryption of sensitive data, and no automated decision-making without human validation. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) to ensure compliance. **Cost Estimation** Based on Nexus Engineering S.r.l. pricing model and target gross margin percentage (28%), Nexus Engineering S.r.l. estimate the total contract value to be 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of approximately 750,000 euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. projected revenue would be 3 million euros, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. projected cost would be 2,160,000 euros. **Sustainability** To contribute to reducing energetic consumption, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. green hosting partners (OVHcloud, Scaleway) and implement digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%. **Conclusion** Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's objectives for an AI assistance tool. a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's objectives for an AI assistance tool ensures explicability, transparency, human oversight, and regulatory compliance while contributing to environmental sustainability and social responsibility. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's objectives for an AI assistance tool will enhance the efficiency of administrative services, improve service quality, and reduce processing times. **Unaddressed Requirements** None of the requirements from the tender are left unaddressed in a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's objectives for an AI assistance tool. However, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. acknowledge that some specific details, such as the exact cost of certain components or the precise timeline for the pilot phase, may require further discussion and clarification with the City of Belval's." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the City of Belval's objectives to improve administrative services' efficiency and quality, and considering our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, how can our company's consolidate all agent contributions into a coherent tender response that meets the City of Belval's objectives to improve administrative services' efficiency and quality? To consolidate agent contributions into a coherent tender response for the City of Belval's, our company's can leverage our company's experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation and AI solutions. our company's project management methodologies, including PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe, can be applied to ensure efficient delivery and high-quality outcomes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

